@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Proposed public Settings API v1
+
+Development proposal; not part of standard 1.7.3. No public version change.
+Implemented in API.lua, with an explicit allowlist of scalar preferences.
+No arbitrary database keys or tables are exposed.
+
+- `Settings.version == 1`: contract version, independent of addon version.
+- `Get(key)`: effective preference, including fallback defaults; nil and reason
+  for unknown keys or an unready database.
+- `Describe(key)`: fresh detached descriptor: type, default, visible, enabled;
+  numeric min/max/step; selection options `{value, label}`. Schema ancestor
+  conditions and dynamic client/unit bounds are evaluated at call time.
+- `Format(key, value)`: uses the settings schema's own text formatter.
+- `Set(key, value)`: true on success, including unchanged values; false and
+  reason on invalid/unknown values. Validates booleans, finite numeric bounds and
+  steps, selection indices and sound IDs (nonnegative integer or blank mute).
+  Uses DBGlobal:SetVariable so normal runtime callbacks run, then invalidates
+  native settings widgets through their normal Setting.Refresh event. It does
+  not invoke widget-specific setters that also write to the database.
+- `OnChange(key, callback)`: one key or `"*"`; returns an unsubscribe function.
+  Callback signature `(key, effectiveValue)`. One internal subscription per
+  allowed key; consumer subscriptions are removable. Consumer exceptions cannot
+  interrupt runtime updates. No polling. Reread dependent descriptors after any
+  notification, including PrefMetric or mode changes.
+- `IsExplicit(key)`: whether the saved table has an own value. Explicit false
+  stays distinct from absent. Nil and reason if unavailable.
+
+Consumers should read fresh on opening, deduplicate writes and respect hidden or
+disabled descriptors. Describe never returns internal schema tables or closures.
+Set validates independently of visibility, permitting programmatic configuration
+of a currently hidden setting.
+
+Global Wipe still requires ReloadUI through the existing native reset path.
+Normal individual changes use SavedVariables.OnChange. The API does not infer
+user intent or override MapPinEnhanced compatibility. It exposes preferences,
+not a promise that a competing renderer is active.
+
+Validation from the companion repository:
+`node tests/run-waypoint-api.js <this-checkout>` executes the actual schema,
+defaults, saved-variable handler, registry and API in fengari. It cannot verify
+rendered widgets, actual sound playback or WoW Forever runtime behavior.
